    {
      "attributes": {
        "description": "Milestone 6.4 (id 72; read its description in full). Started 2026-10-15 at the user's request to keep idle workers busy. FIRST, design and escalate (kind decision, needs_user=true: the milestone says to settle it with the user): what an 'application' is in the record (a new class vs a view over existing entries: federation connection / OIDC client / consumer / service name), with a recommendation and its trade-offs, plus the operation's shape in the operations layer (2.8) and the graph's JSON/DOT form. Build only after the answer. Then (1) the application report/operation (sections per the milestone: identity, directory consumer and ACIs, edge and service names, secrets/keys as references, certificates with expiry, network paths and allowlists, monitors and synthetic checks, recent changes and incidents, owners), built from relations the record already has (blast-radius, dependents, rotation-impact, consumers, canaries, monitors, history); (2) dependency graph JSON + DOT for a component (what depends on it, what it depends on); (3) planner/estate summaries as counts with evidence links (no invented percentages). Everything through the operations layer so 7.1/7.4/7.6 reuse it. RESERVED NUMBERS if a new class is chosen: core attributes 670-679, object classes 140-142 (another worker uses 661-669/137-139). Acceptance per the milestone: report and graph for the showcase's applications, targeted tests, golden diff (the master re-baselines when it is what you predicted), docs. Rules 2991 + 3002. Boundary: the operations layer and the core domain(s) the design picks, CLI command registration for the new report/graph, docs, their tests. Not: cloud adapters, kits, format packages, core environment.py, the planner verdict code (task 523 changes it).",
        "flows": [
          "Showcase & Verification"
        ],
        "name": "6.4 a: application view and dependency graph: design, then the CLI report",
